{"id":173074432768310,"type":"album","name":"Musick to Play in the Dark","artist":"Coil","year":1999,"weight":11,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/53917-musick-to-play-in-the-dark_211439.jpg","aoty":88,"aoty_user":81,"yt":"H7VAlw3d72s","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/coil/musick-to-play-in-the-dark","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/53917-coil-musick-to-play-in-the-dark.php"},"desc":"Musick to Play in the Dark Vol. 1 is a studio album by the British experimental music group Coil, released in September 1999. This album marks a significant shift in the band's musical direction, embracing what they termed \"moon musick\"—a departure from their earlier \"solar\" themes. Musick to Play in the Dark Vol. 1 represents Coil's exploration into \"moon musick,\" characterized by ambient, glitch, minimalism, and kosmische musik influences. This thematic shift signified their transition from \"solar\" to \"moon\" music, embracing elements they previously avoided, such as the feminine, the tidal, and the cyclical. Jhonn Balance provided insights into the ."},"artist_ref":{"id":233770364598869,"name":"Coil","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Coil_band_Portraited.png?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":15318882910861,"type":"genre","name":"Post-Industrial","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":224,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":208607141602166,"name":"RYM Top — Industrial & Noise — Post-Industrial","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":15,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":219177945805128,"name":"RYM Top — Industrial & Noise","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":16,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":150848509715573,"name":"RYM Top — Experimental","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":20,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":1182